add("Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6094", "Character & Manners")
add("Beware of falsehood, for falsehood leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6094", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws (his tongue) and what is between his legs (his chastity), I guarantee for him Paradise.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6474", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6018", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6018", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6018", "Character & Manners")
add("A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hands other Muslims are safe.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 10", "Character & Manners")
add("None of you truly believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 13", "Character & Manners")
add("Allah does not look at your appearance or your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds.", "Sahih Muslim 2564", "Character & Manners")
add("Righteousness is good character, and sin is that which wavers in your heart and you dislike people finding out about it.", "Sahih Muslim 2553", "Character & Manners")
add("Fear Allah wherever you are, follow a bad deed with a good deed and it will erase it, and treat people with good character.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1987", "Character & Manners")
add("Part of the perfection of a person’s Islam is his leaving that which does not concern him.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2317", "Character & Manners")
add("Leave that which makes you doubt for that which does not make you doubt.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2518", "Character & Manners")
add("The believer is simple, noble, and generous, while the wicked person is treacherous and ignoble.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 4790", "Character & Manners")
add("He who does not show mercy to our young ones and recognize the honor of our elders is not one of us.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1919", "Character & Manners")
add("Show mercy to those on earth, and the One in the heavens will show mercy to you.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1924", "Character & Manners")
add("The merciful are shown mercy by the Most Merciful.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1924", "Character & Manners")
add("No one humbles himself for the sake of Allah except that Allah elevates him.", "Sahih Muslim 2588", "Character & Manners")
add("He who has an atom's weight of arrogance in his heart will not enter Paradise. Arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down upon people.", "Sahih Muslim 91", "Character & Manners")
add("Allah is Beautiful and He loves beauty.", "Sahih Muslim 91", "Character & Manners")
add("Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another; be servants of Allah, as brothers.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6064", "Character & Manners")
add("Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6064", "Character & Manners")
add("Do not spy on one another, do not compete maliciously, and do not backbite one another.", "Sahih Muslim 2563", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever conceals the fault of a Muslim, Allah will conceal his faults in this world and the Hereafter.", "Sahih Muslim 2699", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever relieves a believer of a distress in this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress on the Day of Resurrection.", "Sahih Muslim 2699", "Character & Manners")
add("Allah continues to help His servant as long as the servant is helping his brother.", "Sahih Muslim 2699", "Character & Manners")
add("A believer is a mirror to his brother; when he sees a fault in him, he helps him rectify it.", "Al-Adab Al-Mufrad 238", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever defends the honor of his brother in his absence, Allah will protect his face from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1931", "Character & Manners")
add("The true Muslim is gentle, affectionate, and easygoing.", "Musnad Ahmad 20701", "Character & Manners")
add("Purity and clean intentions are the marks of true belief.", "Sahih Muslim 223", "Character & Manners")
add("Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with His anger, nor with the Fire.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 4906", "Character & Manners")
add("A true believer does not taunt, curse, act immorally, or speak filth.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1977", "Character & Manners")
add("Whoever controls his anger while he is able to act upon it, Allah will call him before all creation on the Day of Resurrection to choose any reward he wishes.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 4777", "Character & Manners")
add("If a person gets angry while standing, let him sit down; if his anger leaves him, fine; otherwise, let him lie down.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 4782", "Character & Manners")
add("Anger is from Satan, and Satan was created from fire; fire is extinguished with water, so when one of you gets angry, let him perform Wudu.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 4784", "Character & Manners")
add("Honesty brings tranquility, whereas lying brings doubt and confusion.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2518", "Character & Manners")
add("The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the best to his companion, and the best of neighbors is the best to his neighbor.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1944", "Character & Manners")
add("Kindness is the crown of good character; whoever is deprived of kindness is deprived of all goodness.", "Sahih Muslim 2592", "Character & Manners")
add("Forgive the one who wronged you, join ties with the one who severed them, and do good to the one who harmed you.", "Musnad Ahmad 17334", "Character & Manners")

# --- 6. PATIENCE, GRATITUDE & TRUST IN ALLAH (201-240) ---
add("How wonderful is the affair of the believer! For his affairs are all good: if ease comes to him, he is thankful and that is good for him; and if hardship strikes him, he is patient and that is good for him.", "Sahih Muslim 2999", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("No fatigue, illness, anxiety, grief, hurt, or distress befalls a Muslim, even the prick of a thorn, except that Allah expiates some of his sins by it.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5641", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("True patience is only at the first strike of calamity.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 1283", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Whoever attempts to be patient, Allah will grant him patience. And no one is given a gift better and more vast than patience.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 1469", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Victory comes with patience, relief comes with distress, and with every hardship comes ease.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2516", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Know that what has reached you could never have missed you, and what has missed you could never have reached you.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 4699", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("If the entire creation gathered to benefit you, they could not benefit you except with what Allah has already written for you.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2516", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("If the entire creation gathered to harm you, they could not harm you except with what Allah has already written against you. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2516", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Look at those who are beneath you in worldly matters and do not look at those who are above you; for that is more suitable so that you do not belittle the favors of Allah upon you.", "Sahih Muslim 2963", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("True wealth is not an abundance of worldly goods; true wealth is the wealth of the soul (contentment).", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6446", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Whoever among you wakes up secure in his dwelling, healthy in his body, and having his food for the day, it is as if the whole world has been gathered for him.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2346", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Whoever is not grateful for small blessings will not be grateful for great blessings.", "Musnad Ahmad 18449", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Whoever is not grateful to people is not grateful to Allah.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 4811", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("The greatest reward comes with the greatest trial. When Allah loves a people, He tests them; whoever is content, for him is pleasure, and whoever is discontent, for him is wrath.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2396", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Be mindful of Allah, and He will protect you. Be mindful of Allah, and you will find Him before you.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2516", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Tie your camel and trust in Allah.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2517", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("If you were to rely upon Allah with true reliance, He would provide for you just as He provides for the birds: they go out in the morning hungry and return in the evening full.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2344", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Strive for that which benefits you, seek help from Allah, and do not lose heart. If something befalls you, do not say: 'If only I had done such and such', but say: 'Allah has decreed, and what He willed has happened.'", "Sahih Muslim 2664", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("The word 'if' opens the door to the work of Satan.", "Sahih Muslim 2664", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Patience is light, and prayer is proof.", "Sahih Muslim 223", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("When Allah loves a servant, He tests him with hardships so that He may hear his humble supplication.", "Bayhaqi 9987", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Trials will continue to befall the believing man and woman until they meet Allah with no sin upon them.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2399", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("He who restrains his soul in times of anger and adversity has achieved the highest form of patience.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6114", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Whoever is blessed with contentment will find peace of mind in every situation.", "Musnad Ahmad 17342", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Glad tidings are for the one who was guided to Islam, whose livelihood was sufficient, and who was content with it.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2349", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Be pleased with what Allah has apportioned for you, and you will be the richest of people.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2305", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Treat people well and avoid doing harm, and you will be a true believer.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2305", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Love for people what you love for yourself, and you will be a true Muslim.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2305", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Do not laugh excessively, for excessive laughter deadens the heart.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2305", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("The believer who mixes with people and endures their annoyance has greater reward than the one who does not mix with people and does not endure their annoyance.", "Sunan Ibn Majah 4032", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Allah does not burden a soul beyond that it can bear.", "Surah al-Baqarah 2:286", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Indeed, with hardship comes ease; indeed, with hardship comes ease.", "Surah ash-Sharh 94:5-6", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. And excellent is the final home.", "Surah ar-Ra'd 13:24", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("The reward of gratitude is the increase of blessings: 'If you are grateful, I will surely increase you.'", "Surah Ibrahim 14:7", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Trust in the Living Who does not die, and exalt with His praise.", "Surah al-Furqan 25:58", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Whosoever puts his trust in Allah, He will suffice him.", "Surah at-Talaq 65:3", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Do not grieve; indeed Allah is with us.", "Surah at-Tawbah 9:40", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("The greatest provision for the journey of life is Taqwa (piety) and patience.", "Musnad Ahmad 21542", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Endure patiently; your patience is not except from Allah.", "Surah an-Nahl 16:127", "Patience & Gratitude")
add("Patience is half of faith, and certitude is all of faith.", "Tabarani al-Kabir 8544", "Patience & Gratitude")

# --- 7. REPENTANCE, FORGIVENESS & ALLAH'S MERCY (241-275) ---
add("By Him in Whose hand is my soul, if you did not commit sins, Allah would replace you with a people who commit sins and seek forgiveness from Allah, and He would forgive them.", "Sahih Muslim 2749", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Every son of Adam commits sins, and the best of those who commit sins are those who repent.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2499", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("The one who repents from sin is like one who had no sin.", "Sunan Ibn Majah 4250", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Allah the Almighty said: O son of Adam, so long as you call upon Me and ask of Me, I shall forgive you for what you have done, and I shall not mind.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3540", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("O son of Adam, were your sins to reach the clouds of the sky and were you then to ask forgiveness of Me, I would forgive you.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3540", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("O son of Adam, were you to come to Me with sins nearly as great as the earth and were you then to face Me, ascribing no partner to Me, I would bring you forgiveness nearly as great as it.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3540", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Allah is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you would be who lost his camel in a barren desert, then unexpectedly found it.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6309", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Allah stretches out His hand at night to accept the repentance of those who sinned during the day, and He stretches out His hand during the day to accept the repentance of those who sinned during the night, until the sun rises from the west.", "Sahih Muslim 2759", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Whoever repents before the sun rises from the west, Allah will accept his repentance.", "Sahih Muslim 2703", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Allah accepts the repentance of a servant as long as the death rattle has not reached his throat.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3537", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Verily, My mercy overcomes My anger.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 7553", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Allah divided mercy into one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine parts with Himself and sent down one single part to earth; by that single part, all creatures show compassion to one another.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6000", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Allah is more merciful to His servants than a mother is to her infant child.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5999", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("I seek the forgiveness of Allah and turn to Him in repentance more than seventy times a day.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6307", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Whoever constantly seeks forgiveness, Allah will appoint for him a way out of every distress, relief from every anxiety, and provide for him from where he does not expect.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 1518", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins.", "Surah az-Zumar 39:53", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("No soul that repents with sincerity will ever be rejected by the Most Merciful.", "Riyad as-Salihin 14", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("When a servant admits his sin and repents, Allah turns to him with forgiveness.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 2661", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Remorse is the heart of repentance.", "Sunan Ibn Majah 4252", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Forgive people, and Allah will forgive you. Overlook their shortcomings, and Allah will overlook yours.", "Musnad Ahmad 7001", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven.", "Musnad Ahmad 19284", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("He who pardons and reconciles, his reward is directly with Allah.", "Surah ash-Shura 42:40", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("The Prophet never took revenge for a personal matter; he only acted when the limits of Allah were violated.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6853", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Do not hold grudges against your brothers; the gates of Paradise open on Monday and Thursday and every servant is forgiven except two who have enmity between them.", "Sahih Muslim 2565", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Cleanse your heart before sleeping each night from any ill will toward any Muslim.", "Sunan an-Nasa'i 10699", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("The gates of repentance remain open wide until the final breath.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3537", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Seek forgiveness for your mistakes, for none of us is free from error.", "Sunan Ibn Majah 4250", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("When you commit a wrong, immediately follow it with an act of worship or kindness.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1987", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Allah loves the persistent servant who turns back to Him again and again.", "Bayhaqi 7120", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("No sin is too great for the mercy of the Lord of the worlds.", "Sahih Muslim 2758", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Tears shed in fear or love of Allah will never touch the Hellfire.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1633", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Two eyes will not be touched by the Fire: an eye that weeps out of fear of Allah, and an eye that stands guard in the way of Allah.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1639", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Repentance cleanses the rust of sins from the heart.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3334", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("The door of Tawbah is broader than the distance between heaven and earth.", "Tabarani 7431", "Repentance & Mercy")
add("Never think that Allah will not forgive you; despair in Allah's mercy is among the greatest wrongs.", "Musnad Ahmad 434", "Repentance & Mercy")

# --- 8. FAMILY, PARENTS & KINSHIP (276-305) ---
add("A man asked: O Messenger of Allah, who is most deserving of my fine companionship? The Prophet said: 'Your mother.' The man asked: Then who? He said: 'Your mother.' The man asked: Then who? He said: 'Your mother.' The man asked: Then who? He said: 'Your father.'", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5971", "Family & Kinship")
add("Paradise lies beneath the feet of mothers.", "Sunan an-Nasa'i 3104", "Family & Kinship")
add("The pleasure of the Lord is in the pleasure of the parents, and the displeasure of the Lord is in the displeasure of the parents.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1899", "Family & Kinship")
add("The best of you are those who are best to their families, and I am the best among you to my family.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3895", "Family & Kinship")
add("Whoever desires an expansion in his sustenance and an extension in his lifespan, let him uphold ties of kinship.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5986", "Family & Kinship")
add("The one who upholds family ties is not merely the one who responds in kind, but the one who joins ties when they have been severed.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5991", "Family & Kinship")
add("The tie of kinship (Rahim) clings to the Throne of the Almighty, saying: 'Whoever keeps me, Allah will keep him; and whoever severs me, Allah will sever him.'", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5989", "Family & Kinship")
add("The one who severs ties of kinship will not enter Paradise.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5984", "Family & Kinship")
add("Treat your children with equality and fairness.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 2587", "Family & Kinship")
add("Whoever raises two daughters until they reach maturity, he and I will enter Paradise together like this — and he brought his fingers together.", "Sahih Muslim 2631", "Family & Kinship")
add("The father is the middle door of Paradise; so keep that door or lose it.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1900", "Family & Kinship")
add("No father can give his child a better gift than good manners and noble upbringing.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 1952", "Family & Kinship")
add("Kindness to parents is second only to prayer in the sight of Allah.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 527", "Family & Kinship")
add("Even if your parents hold different views or faiths, treat them with utmost gentleness and honor.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5978", "Family & Kinship")
add("A woman is married for four things: wealth, lineage, beauty, and piety. Seek the one with piety, may your hands be blessed.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5090", "Family & Kinship")
add("The whole world is provision, and the best provision of this world is a righteous spouse.", "Sahih Muslim 1467", "Family & Kinship")
add("A believing man should not hate a believing woman; if he dislikes one of her traits, he will be pleased with another.", "Sahih Muslim 1469", "Family & Kinship")
add("Feed your wife, clothe her as you clothe yourself, and do not insult her or strike her.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 2142", "Family & Kinship")
add("Play with your children, show them affection, and kiss them often.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5997", "Family & Kinship")
add("A man saw the Prophet kissing his grandchild and said: 'I have ten children and have never kissed any of them.' The Prophet looked at him and said: 'He who does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.'", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5997", "Family & Kinship")
add("Honoring a father's friends after his passing is among the finest acts of filial piety.", "Sahih Muslim 2552", "Family & Kinship")
add("Your relatives have rights over you, and your spouse has rights over you; so give each their rightful due.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 1968", "Family & Kinship")
add("The most blessed marriage is the one with the easiest expenses.", "Musnad Ahmad 24595", "Family & Kinship")
add("Do not overlook the small joys and peaceful moments spent with your family.", "Al-Adab Al-Mufrad 78", "Family & Kinship")
add("Make your home a place of light by praying voluntary prayers inside it and reciting the Qur’an.", "Sahih Muslim 777", "Family & Kinship")
add("A house in which the Qur’an is recited shines for the dwellers of heaven just as stars shine for dwellers of earth.", "Bayhaqi 1983", "Family & Kinship")
add("Honor your elderly parents, for having them in your life is an open gate to Jannah.", "Sahih Muslim 2551", "Family & Kinship")
add("May his nose be rubbed in dust, the one whose parents reach old age in his lifetime and he does not enter Paradise.", "Sahih Muslim 2551", "Family & Kinship")
add("A mother’s supplication for her child is swift to be answered.", "Sunan Ibn Majah 3862", "Family & Kinship")
add("Speak to your parents with words of honor and lower the wing of humility to them.", "Surah al-Isra 17:23-24", "Family & Kinship")

# --- 9. KNOWLEDGE, WISDOM & QUR'AN (306-335) ---
add("The best among you are those who learn the Qur’an and teach it.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5027", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Whoever takes a path seeking knowledge, Allah will make easy for him a path to Paradise.", "Sahih Muslim 2699", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim.", "Sunan Ibn Majah 224", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("The angels lower their wings over the seeker of knowledge out of pleasure for what he is doing.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 3641", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like the superiority of the full moon over all other heavenly bodies.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 3641", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("The scholars are the inheritors of the Prophets.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 3641", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Whoever recites a single letter from the Book of Allah will receive one good deed, and that good deed is multiplied tenfold.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2910", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("The one who is proficient in the Qur’an will be with the noble, obedient angels; and the one who recites the Qur’an and stutters in it, finding it difficult, will have a double reward.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 4937", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Beautify the Qur’an with your voices, for a melodious voice increases the Qur’an in beauty.", "Sunan Abi Dawud 1468", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Do not envy anyone except in two cases: a person to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it rightfully, and a person to whom Allah has given wisdom and he acts according to it and teaches it.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 73", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Whoever guides someone to a good deed will have a reward equal to the one who performs it.", "Sahih Muslim 1893", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Convey from me, even if it is a single verse.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 3461", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears my words, comprehends them, memorizes them, and conveys them to others.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2657", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Wisdom is the lost property of the believer; wherever he finds it, he has the greatest right to it.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2687", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("O Allah, benefit me through what You have taught me, teach me that which will benefit me, and increase me in knowledge.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3599", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Seek refuge in Allah from knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satisfied, and a prayer that is not answered.", "Sahih Muslim 2722", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("The example of guidance and knowledge with which Allah has sent me is like abundant rain falling on the earth.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 79", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("A single scholar of deep insight is harder on Satan than a thousand worshippers.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2681", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Learn your religion, teach it to people, and act with humility before your teachers.", "Tabarani 6184", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("The heart that contains nothing of the Qur’an is like an abandoned, ruined house.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2913", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Read the Qur’an regularly, for by Him in Whose hand is my soul, it escapes faster than a tied camel.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 5033", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("It will be said to the companion of the Qur’an on the Day of Judgment: 'Recite and ascend; recite as you used to recite in the world, for your rank is at the last verse you recite.'", "Sunan Abi Dawud 1464", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Surah al-Mulk protects its reader from the punishment of the grave.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2891", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Whoever desires the honor of this world and the next, let him hold firmly to the Book of Allah.", "Sahih Muslim 817", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("The best form of wealth after faith is beneficial knowledge that lights your path.", "Musnad Ahmad 12044", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Reflect upon the verses of the Qur’an, for in reflection lies the renewal of faith.", "Bayhaqi 2145", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Actions must be guided by knowledge, and knowledge must be adorned with humility.", "Al-Adab Al-Mufrad 143", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Knowledge without practice is like a tree without fruit.", "Bayhaqi 1892", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("When Allah wishes good for a person, He grants him deep comprehension of the religion.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 71", "Knowledge & Wisdom")
add("Ask the people of knowledge if you do not know.", "Surah an-Nahl 16:43", "Knowledge & Wisdom")

# --- 10. RIGHTEOUS DEEDS, PARADISE & CONSISTENCY (336-370) ---
add("The most beloved deeds to Allah are those that are done consistently, even if they are small.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6464", "Righteous Deeds")
add("Take up good deeds only as much as you are able, for Allah does not tire of rewarding until you tire of doing.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 586", "Righteous Deeds")
add("Do not delay good deeds, for tomorrow is not promised to anyone.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6416", "Righteous Deeds")
add("Take benefit of five before five: your youth before your old age, your health before your sickness, your wealth before your poverty, your free time before your preoccupation, and your life before your death.", "Shu'ab al-Iman 9575", "Righteous Deeds")
add("Be in this world as though you were a stranger or a traveler passing through.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6416", "Righteous Deeds")
add("When you wake in the morning, do not wait for the evening; and when evening comes, do not wait for the morning. Take from your health for your sickness, and from your life for your death.", "Sahih al-Bukhari 6416", "Righteous Deeds")
add("This world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever.", "Sahih Muslim 2956", "Righteous Deeds")
add("What is this world to me? The likeness of me and this world is only like a rider who rested in the shade of a tree on a hot day, then moved on and left it.", "Jami at-Tirmidhi 2377", "Righteous Deeds")
